course: french
lesson: 23
title: Hobbies and sport
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: French uses three different patterns for what you do in your free time: jouer à for sports and games, jouer de for musical instruments, and faire de for activities like cycling, swimming or judo.
explain: So you say je joue au football, but je joue du piano, and je fais du vélo - a bit like how English says "play football" but "go cycling".
explain: Picture a sunny campsite in the south of France: grandads and kids throw heavy metal balls at a tiny wooden one called le cochonnet, the piglet, and shout "Bravo !" when one lands close - that is la pétanque.
explain: When you like doing something, the doing word stays in its base form after j'aime: j'aime danser, j'aime nager, j'aime lire - never "j'aime dance".
explain: Young French people say "C'est trop bien !" when something is really great, and in the playground they shout "On joue à chat !", which is tag, not a game about pets.
fact: For sports and games French says jouer à: je joue au football, je joue au tennis, je joue aux cartes.
fact: For musical instruments French says jouer de: je joue du piano, je joue de la guitare, je joue du violon.
fact: Some activities use faire de: je fais du vélo (I go cycling), je fais de la natation (I go swimming), je fais du judo, je fais du surf; if you don't know the verb for a sport, je fais du + the sport (je fais du skate) is a safe trick.
fact: Some sports have their own verb: nager means to swim, so je nage means I swim.
fact: C'est trop bien ! is casual and means "It's really good!"; trop on its own usually means too much.
fact: La pétanque is a French game of throwing metal balls close to a small wooden ball called le cochonnet (the piglet); children play it too.
fact: Je lis means I read; it comes from lire and the s is silent, so it sounds like "zhuh LEE".
fact: Popular sports in France include football, rugby, tennis, cycling, handball and judo; baseball is rare there.
fact: The Tour de France is a famous cycling race held every July that finishes in Paris.
fact: Le maillot jaune is the yellow jersey worn by the rider leading the whole race, not a team colour.
fact: After j'aime the verb stays in its base form: j'aime danser, j'aime nager, j'aime lire.
fact: In France tag is called chat: "On joue à chat !" means "Let's play tag!", and whoever is "it" is le chat.
fact: Other playground games: cache-cache (hide and seek) and la marelle (hopscotch).
exercise: How do you say "I play football"? | Je joue au football | Je joue football | Je joue du football | Je fais au football
exercise: Ava plays the piano. What does she say? | Je joue du piano | Je joue au piano | Je fais au piano | Je joue piano
exercise: Which pattern goes with musical instruments? | jouer de | jouer à | faire à | aimer de
exercise: Liam goes cycling. Which is right? | Je fais du vélo | Je joue au vélo | Je joue du vélo | Je vélo
exercise: Kai says "Je surf". What should he say? | Je fais du surf | Je joue au surf | Je surfe du | Je joue de surf
exercise: What does je nage mean? | I swim | I sail | I skate | I sing
exercise: Olivia's penpal writes "C'est trop bien !" How does she feel? | Really happy about it | Fed up, it's too much | Bored, it's just okay | Worried, it's too hard
exercise: What is le cochonnet in pétanque? | The small wooden ball you aim at | The heavy metal ball you throw | The lucky player who wins | The flat ground you play on
exercise: How does je lis sound? | zhuh LEE, with a silent s | zhuh LISS, with a hissing s | zhuh LIZZ, with a buzzing s | zhuh LICE, rhyming with nice
exercise: Mason's French friend asks "Le baseball, c'est quoi ?" Why? | Baseball is rare in France | Baseball is banned in France | Mason said the word wrong | French children only play rugby
exercise: When does the Tour de France take place? | Every July | Every December | Every April | Every four years
exercise: Who wears le maillot jaune? | The rider leading the whole race | The rider in the yellow team | The slowest rider in the race | The rider who won last year
exercise: Ruby likes dancing. Which is right? | J'aime danser | J'aime dance | J'aime dansing | J'aime la danser
exercise: Theo hears "On joue à chat !" What happens next? | They chase each other in a game of tag | They all pretend to be cats and miaow | They go and look for the school cat | They sit down and draw pictures of cats
exercise: What is cache-cache? | Hide and seek | Hopscotch | Tag | Skipping
exercise: Which sentence is right? | Je joue de la guitare | Je joue à la guitare | Je fais la guitare | Je joue guitare
test: Your mate goes, "Bruv, it's je joue du football, same as piano, innit." Put him right. | Sport takes à: je joue au football | He's right, du works for everything | It's je fais au football | It's je joue football with no little word
test: Gemma from Cardiff says, "Tidy, so I play the flute: je joue à la flûte." (tidy = nice, great) What's right? | Je joue de la flûte | Je joue à la flûte | Je fais à la flûte | Je joue au flûte
test: A cartoon kid says "Je joue de la natation". Your sister says, "That's well dodgy." Fix it. | Je fais de la natation | Je joue à la natation | Je joue du natation | Je natation
test: Ethan says, "Pétanque? That's just for old blokes in flat caps, like." Is he right? | No, children play it too | Yes, children are not allowed | Yes, it is only played in cafés | No, it's only for children
test: What would happen if you said "C'est trop !" instead of "C'est trop bien !" about a film? | You'd sound like it was too much, not that it was great | It would mean exactly the same thing | You'd sound like the film was very short | It would mean the film was rubbish but funny
test: Your brother says the yellow jersey in the Tour de France means you're in the yellow team, no cap. (no cap = honestly) What's true? | It goes to the rider leading the whole race | He's right, the yellow team wears it | It goes to the youngest rider | It goes to the rider who fell off most
test: ★★★ Which sentence has ALL three patterns right? | Je joue au tennis, je joue du violon et je fais du judo | Je joue du tennis, je joue au violon et je fais du judo | Je joue au tennis, je joue au violon et je joue au judo | Je fais du tennis, je joue au violon et je joue du judo
test: Sophie from Edinburgh reads "Je lis" as "liss" and her pal goes, "Aye, sounds right tae me, hen." What should they know? | The s is silent: zhuh LEE | The s is said like z: zhuh LIZZ | The s is doubled: zhuh LISS | The i is long: zhuh LICE
test: ★★★ A French girl says "J'aime nager et je fais du vélo, mais je ne joue pas au foot." Which is true about her? | She swims and cycles but doesn't play football | She plays football but doesn't swim or cycle | She cycles to football but can't swim | She swims at football practice on her bike
test: Kai from Auckland goes, "Chur, sweet as, I'll make up a verb: je skate." (chur = thanks, cool) What's the safe trick when you don't know the verb? | Use je fais du + the sport | Add an -o to the English word | Use je joue de + the sport | Just say the English word louder
test: ★★★ Hopscotch, tag and hide and seek - which list matches them in order? | la marelle, chat, cache-cache | chat, la marelle, cache-cache | cache-cache, chat, la marelle | la marelle, cache-cache, chat
exam: Identify the construction prescribed in French for the playing of a musical instrument. | jouer de | jouer à | faire à | jouer sans préposition
exam: Select the correct rendering of the statement "I engage in cycling" in the French language. | Je fais du vélo | Je joue au vélo | Je joue du vélo | Je fais au vélo
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises le maillot jaune in the Tour de France? | The jersey worn by the rider leading the overall race | The jersey worn by every member of a designated team | The jersey awarded to the rider finishing last | The jersey worn exclusively on the final day
exam: Determine the form of the verb required subsequent to j'aime in the statement "I like dancing". | danser, the base form | dance, the English form | danse, the present form | dansant, the -ing form
